{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_fsm_persistent_fsm_persistentfsm", "label": "PersistentFSM", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Table-driven and event-sourced: every command that fires a transition persists its events, and a restart replays them through applyEvent to resume the exact state name and data.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/fsm/persistent-fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_fsm_persistent_fsm_fsmtransitionmap", "label": "FsmTransitionMap transition table", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "State by command kind to an entry with an event, a target next and an optional guard. Declared as a class field so per-command type narrowing works at each call site; next is mainly informational since applyEvent drives the transition, but a mismatch is warned to catch table and fold drift.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/fsm/persistent-fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_fsm_persistent_fsm_applyevent", "label": "applyEvent pure fold", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The single source of truth for state and data updates. It runs both at persist time and during recovery, so it must be deterministic and free of side effects; transitions and guards are consulted only for live commands.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/fsm/persistent-fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_fsm_persistent_fsm_recovery", "label": "PersistentFSM recovery", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "preStart loads the latest snapshot and reads every subsequent domain event, replays them in order through applyEvent, then fires onRecoveryComplete. A failed recovery stops the FSM before any transition runs or any state timeout is armed.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/fsm/persistent-fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_fsm_persistent_fsm_multi_event_transition", "label": "Multi-event transitions", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "An array of events persists atomically in one persistAll, applyEvent runs once per event, and only the final post-replay state is checked against next; an empty array is a no-op. tagsFor is asked once per event too.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/fsm/persistent-fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_fsm_persistent_fsm_state_timeout", "label": "State timeouts", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A _timeout entry arms a one-shot timer on entering a state and fires its event through the same persist-then-apply pipeline. On recovery the timer is re-armed relative to wall-clock at recovery completion, so a long-stopped FSM gets a fresh window rather than an immediate expiry.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/fsm/persistent-fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_fsm_persistent_fsm_timeout_rearm_supersedes", "label": "Re-arming supersedes a queued timeout fire", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A fired timeout travels through the mailbox like any message, so it can already be queued behind an unprocessed command; re-arming on every transition, including one that stays in the same state, drops the superseded fire instead of expiring a session that was just renewed.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/fsm/persistent-fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_fsm_persistent_fsm_side_effects_in_oncommand", "label": "Side effects belong in onCommand", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "PersistentFSM has no enter, exit or transition hooks; onCommand never runs during replay, so overriding it and acting after super is what makes a side effect fire once per real transition rather than on every restart.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/fsm/persistent-fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_fsm_persistent_fsm_no_stay_data_channel", "label": "There is no stay for data-only updates", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A command with no matching transition entry is dropped and the in-memory data is not mutated as a side channel; a data-only update that must survive a restart is modelled as an event whose next is the same state.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/fsm/persistent-fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_fsm_persistent_fsm_persistence_id_collision", "label": "persistenceId collision with another actor", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "PersistentFSM and PersistentActor share the journal, so the same persistenceId is the same event stream; use distinct ids rather than discovering the clash at replay.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/fsm/persistent-fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_fsm_persistent_fsm_persistentfsm", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_fsm_persistent_fsm_fsmtransitionmap", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": 